      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STRATFORD (2) couldn't quite live up to expectations on debut but made a promising start nevertheless when charging home for third at Gosford. The step to 1400m suits and he looks the one to beat with that run under his belt. MARKOS PORT (1) attracted no support on debut at Hawkesbury but was strong late to also grab third. Natural improvement and the added trip make him very interesting. SCOISH MALOISH (6) resumes from a short break after placing at Canterbury and Gosford on soft ground. A Warwick Farm trial gives him a solid base for this return. INVASION (4) didn't fire a shot on debut after trialling well in readiness. Suspect that was too bad to be true and he can improve sharply with that run under the belt.",
